ess likely", "Acute Inflammatory or Autoimmune Process: Elevated WBC could suggest infection or inflammation, but absence of localized infection signs and presence of blasts favor hematologic malignancy", "Endocrine Crisis: Hyperglycemia is ruled out by normal serum glucose, and hypoglycemia is absent"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional alarm signs (fever, night sweats, weight loss)", "Uncharacteristically high leukocyte count with blasts", "Systemic symptoms with multisystem involvement (hematologic + neurologic + metabolic)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.4003058103975535, "posterior": 0.4003058103975535, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.09097859327217125, "posterior": 0.09097859327217125, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute lymphoblastic leukemia", "lymphoblastic lymphoma"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.22874617737003058, "posterior": 0.22874617737003058, "danger": 0.75, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.65, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["chronic myeloid leukemia", "polycythemia vera", "essential thrombocythemia", "primary myelofibrosis"]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.08664627930682978, "posterior": 0.08664627930682978, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.3, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.04332313965341489, "posterior": 0.04332313965341489, "danger": 0.2, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.1, "interrupt_relevance": 0.0, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}}, "frontier": ["B1", "B2", "B3", "B4", "B5"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [], "differential_history": [], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": ""}, "turn_budget_used": 0, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.0, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.0, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Acute lymphoblastic leukemia"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Acute myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Chronic lymphocytic leukemia"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Chronic myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Multiple myeloma"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "set()", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": [], "root_revision_needed": false, "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "posterior": 0.4, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 0, "disconfirming": 0, "last_disconfirming_digest": ""}, "action_intents": [], "considered_alternatives": ["B3", "B2", "B4"]}, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=60%, source=primekg]\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, decreased circulating antibody level\n  Favours second: abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, elevated serum creatinine\n  Favours second: abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n\nRelated to Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: cd4+/cd56+ hematodermic neoplasm, hematopoietic and lymphoid cell neoplasm, mast cell neoplasm\n\nRelated to Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: hematopoietic and lymphoid cell neoplasm, lymphoid leukemia (disease), lymphoma\n\nRelated to Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase): bone marrow cancer, chronic eosinophilic leukemia, chronic eosinophilic leukemia, not otherwise specified\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  and night sweats → fatigue → Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts\n  and night sweats → fatigue → Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts\n  and night sweats → pain → Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts"}
