s less likely", "Acute Inflammatory or Autoimmune Process: Elevated WBC could suggest infection or inflammation, but absence of localized infection signs and presence of blasts favor hematologic malignancy", "Endocrine Crisis: Hyperglycemia is ruled out by normal serum glucose, and hypoglycemia is absent", "Myeloproliferative Disorder: Considered but not elevated due to competing differential of lymphoproliferative/plasma cell disorder"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional alarm signs (fever, night sweats, weight loss)", "Uncharacteristically high leukocyte count with blasts", "Systemic symptoms with multisystem involvement (hematologic + neurologic + metabolic)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0544346421162868, "posterior": 0.03216059624833023, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The combination of blasts in leukocytosis and systemic symptoms like fever and weight loss is more typical of myeloid neoplasms (e.g., AML) than chronic or lym…"], "evidence_against": ["The subacute onset and systemic symptoms (e.g., ataxia) are less typical of myeloid neoplasms but do not decisively exclude them."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.38918880577401876, "posterior": 0.1955850701962471, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The lack of lymphoid-specific features (e.g., skin changes) weakens the case for lymphoid neoplasms but does not exclude them entirely."], "evidence_against": ["The combination of blasts in leukocytosis and systemic symptoms like fever and weight loss is more typical of myeloid neoplasms (e.g., AML) than chronic or lym…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute lymphoblastic leukemia", "lymphoblastic lymphoma"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.28137448115354646, "danger": 0.75, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["35% blasts in leukocytosis is the strongest evidence against chronic myeloproliferative neoplasms, which rarely exceed 10% blasts without transformation."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B3.1", "B3.2", "B3.3", "B3.4"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.65, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["chronic myeloid leukemia", "polycythemia vera", "essential thrombocythemia", "primary myelofibrosis"]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.149, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Normal calcium levels reduce the likelihood of multiple myeloma but are not definitive exclusion criteria for plasma cell disorders."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.018, "danger": 0.2, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_re